                  %use{:x => "46.506542", "xlink:href" => "#wsh1IqsgGI0LOrCwwHd1H7MG7PA=-glyph3-2", :y => "108.045725"}
            %p
              The corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
              is also known (at least when
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
              is regarded as a category of “spaces”) as the category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mi ℛ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}_{\mathcal{R}}
              of “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retractive+spaces"}> retractive spaces
              ” in
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒮
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mi ℛ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒮
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi ℬ
                    %msup
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{S}_{\mathcal{R}}
                    \\;\;\;
                    \\simeq
                    \\;\;\;
                    \\int_{B \in \mathcal{S}}
                    \\big(
                    \\mathcal{S}_{/\mathcal{B}}
                    \\big)^{\ast/}
                    \\,.
            %p
              This follows readily from the definitions, but see also
              = succeed ";" do
                %a{:href => "retractive+space#BraunackMayer19"} Braunack-Mayer (2021), Rem. 1.15
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "retractive+space#HebestreitSagaveSchlichtkrull20"} Hebestreit, Sagave &amp; Schlichtkrull (2020), Lem. 2.14
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+parameterized+spectra"} model category-presentation
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"}
                tangent
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              of (the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+localization"} simplicial localization
              of)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒮
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
          %p
            In alternative slight variation of Exp.
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SliceCategoriesAndArrowCategory"}
          %p
          #AbelianizedSlicesAndTangentCategory.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (abelianized slice categories and tangent category)
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
              a category with
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mi op
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Ab\big(
                    \\mathcal{S}_{/(-)}
                    \\big)
                    \\;\;
                    \\colon
                    \\;\;
                    \\mathcal{S}^{op}
                    \\longrightarrow
                    Cat
            %p
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contravariant+functor"} contravariant
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudofunctor"} pseudofunctor
              which sends
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  any
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒮
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \in \mathcal{S}
                  to the category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Ab
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒮
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi B
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab\big(\mathcal{S}_{/B}\big)
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+objects"} group objects
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
                  to the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒮
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}_{/B}
              %li
                %p
                  any
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi B
                        %mo →
                        %mi B
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon B \to B'
                  to the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi Ab
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒮
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi B
                            %mo ′
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi Ab
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒮
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi B
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast \colon Ab\big(\mathcal{S}_{/B'}\big) \to Ab\big(\mathcal{S}_{/B}\big)
                  given by
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  (which
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preserved+limit"} preserves
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+objects"} group objects
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
              on this functor may be called the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+category"} tangent category
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒮
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+elements"} category of elements
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-sided+fibration"} two-sided fibration
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+Grothendieck+construction"} indexed Grothendieck construction
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-Grothendieck+construction"}> 2-Grothendieck construction
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category+of+elements"} 2-category of elements
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-Grothendieck+construction"} (infinity,1)-Grothendieck construction
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction+for+monoidal+categories"} Grothendieck construction for monoidal categories
          %h2#references References
          %p The Grothendieck construction originates in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Grothendieck"}> Alexander Grothendieck
              , §VI.8 of:
              %em Revêtements Étales et Groupe Fondamental - Séminaire de Géometrie Algébrique du Bois Marie 1960/61
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SGA+1"}> SGA 1
              ) , LNM
              %strong 224
              Springer (1971) &amp;lbrack;updated version with comments by M. Raynaud:
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0206203"} arxiv.0206203
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Angelo+Vistoli"}> Angelo Vistoli
              , §3.1.3 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Grothendieck topologies, fibered categories and descent theory
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fundamental+algebraic+geometry+--+Grothendieck%27s+FGA+explained"} Fundamental algebraic geometry – Grothendieck's FGA explained
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 123
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/surv-123-s"} ISBN:978-0-8218-4245-4
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0412512"} math.AG/0412512
          %p Further textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
                , Section 8.3 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Categorical+Algebra"} Handbook of Categorical Algebra
                %em Categories and Structures
                Encyclopedia of Mathematics and its Applications
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 50
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511525865"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511525865
            %li#Johnstone
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
                , sections A1.1.7, B1.3.1 of:
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sketches+of+an+Elephant"} Sketches of an Elephant
                (2002)
            %li#Warner12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Garth+Warner"}> Garth Warner
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Fibrations and Sheaves
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://hdl.handle.net/1773/20977"} hdl:1773/20977
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://sites.math.washington.edu//~warner/Warner_FIBRATIONS%20AND%20SHEAVES.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Warner-FibrationsAndSheaves.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#JohnsonYau20
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Niles+Johnson"}> Niles Johnson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Donald+Yau"} Donald Yau
                = succeed "," do
                  %em 2-Dimensional Categories
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/2002.06055"} arXiv:2002.06055
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://oxford.universitypressscholarship.com/view/10.1093/oso/9780198871378.001.0001/oso-9780198871378"} doi:10.1093/oso/9780198871378.001.0001
          %p
            Survey in the generality of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category"} internal-
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category+theory"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              \-category theory
            (see also the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+Grothendieck+construction"} enriched-
              and
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-Grothendieck+construction"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                  \-Grothendieck construction
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Liang+Ze+Wong"}> Liang Ze Wong
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Grothendieck Construction in Enriched, Internal and ∞-Category Theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://sheaves.github.io/slides/thesis.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Wong-GrothendieckConstruction.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization+of+categories"} geometric realization
            of Grothendieck constructions has been analyzed in
          %ul
            %li#Thomason79
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/R.+W.+Thomason"}> R. W. Thomason
              ,
              %em Homotopy colimits in the category of small categories
              , Math. Proc. Cambridge Philos. Soc. 85 (1979), no. 1, 91109.
          %p The left adjoint to the Grothendieck construction is discussed in §3.1.1 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Georges+Maltsiniotis"}> Georges Maltsiniotis
              ,
              %em La théorie de l’homotopie de Grothendieck
          %p On limits and colimits in Grothendieck constructions:
          %ul
            %li#TBG91
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrzej+Tarlecki"}> Andrzej Tarlecki
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rod+M.+Burstall"} Rod M. Burstall
